Hoisted the vector's data pointer and size out of the loop and removed the repeated `operator[]`/`size()` calls, giving the compiler a tighter pointer-walk that it can keep in registers.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* const base = fields.data();
    const int n = (int)fields.size();
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
    {
        if (base[i].GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return &base[i];
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```